# Kconfig for the balloon pressure test rig

config MEASUREMENT_INTERVAL
    int "Measurement interval in seconds"
    default 30
    range 5 3600
    help
        How often to read pressure and temperature from the sensor.
        Default: 30 seconds (short test).
        For long-term tests: 300 seconds (5 minutes).

menu "Over-pressure interlock"

config BALLOON_IL_DP_CUTOFF_MBAR
    int "Differential-pressure cut-off (mbar, P_internal - P_ambient)"
    default 5
    range 1 200
    help
        PLACEHOLDER — NOT a validated ceiling.  Hard ceiling on the differential
        pressure across the envelope wall.  When exceeded, the interlock closes
        the (normally-closed) fill valve and raises the alarm.

        The envelope is NOT a pressure vessel and is NOT rated to a burst
        pressure: the protocol's control variable is CIRCUMFERENCE, not
        pressure.  This cut-off is a GROSS over-inflation detector, not a
        working setpoint.  Its number must be derived from a bench
        characterisation of differential pressure vs circumference
        (docs/PRESTRETCH-OVERPRESSURE-INTERLOCK.md, bench session B1) before
        anyone treats it as real.

config BALLOON_IL_DP_RESET_MBAR
    int "Differential pressure required before a reset is allowed (mbar)"
    default 2
    range 0 200
    help
        A latched trip may only be cleared once the differential has fallen
        back below this value AND the sensor is healthy.  Must be <= the
        cut-off above.

config BALLOON_IL_MAX_FILL_S
    int "Hard fill-time ceiling (seconds)"
    default 10800
    range 60 86400
    help
        Redundant backstop against a stuck-open fill valve: the fill is closed
        after this many seconds regardless of pressure.  10800 s = 3 h.

endmenu
